      "status": "completed",
      "text": "The glass doors of the Fulcrum research facility slid open, and Mara stepped out into the evening light. The city's glow cast long shadows, painting the sidewalks with amber hues. Her mind replayed the oppressive session, the questions designed to expose every insecurity. Jonah, ever composed, trailed behind her, his footsteps deliberate on the concrete.\n\nAs the door's hiss faded, she turned, still sorting through the raw emotions left behind. He offered his hand, a silent offer. No interpretation, no manipulation—just a choice. Her fingers brushed against his, warm and steady, a tether to the present. For the first time since entering that sterile lab, she felt anchored.",
