      "status": "completed",
      "text": "Esther stepped into Simon's bedroom, her gaze catching on the open novel on the nightstand. He was engrossed in a passage, the dim light casting soft shadows on his face.\n“You're still reading?” she teased, crossing to him with a smile. “I thought we agreed to take it easy tonight.”\nSimon looked up, the corners of his lips quirking in response. “Well, I might need some reading material if this gets too intense.”\nHis teasing tone eased the tension that had been lingering since their reunion. They had faced danger together, but it was the unspoken moments, the unacknowledged doubts, that had made intimacy feel like a minefield.\n“Oh, are we going that route?” Esther replied, her voice dripping with mock indignation. “Maybe I'll just grab a book and leave you to your reading then.”",
